    rdfs:label "oculopharyngodistal myopathy 2"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "An oculopharyngodistal myopathy that is characterized by onset of distal muscle weakness, mainly of the lower limbs, and/or ophthalmoplegia in the second or third decades of life, and that has_material_basis_in heterozygous trinucleotide repeat expansion (GGC(n)) in the 5-prime untranslated region (UTR) of the GIPC1 gene on chromosome 19p13."@en ;
