obo:DOID_13117 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "paronychia"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A nail disease characterized by often-tender bacterial or fungal hand infection or foot infection due to either bacteria or fungus (Candida albicans) where the nail and skin meet at the side or the base of a finger or toe nail. The infection can start suddenly (acute paronychia) or gradually (chronic paronychia). Puss is usually present, along with gradual thickening and browning discoloration of the nail plate."@en ;
