obo:DOID_13523 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "loiasis"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A filariasis that involves parasitic infection of the skin and eyes caused by the nematode Loa loa, which is transmitted through the bite of a deer fly or mango fly. The disease is characterized by episodic angioedema in the arms and legs, and cyst-like enlargements of the connective tissue around the sheaths of muscle tendons. Dead worms may cause chronic abscesses, which may lead to the formation of granulomatous reactions and fibrosis."@en ;
    oboInOwl:hasDbXref "GARD:3283",
        "ICD10CM:B74.3",
        "ICD9CM:125.2",
        "MESH:D008118",
        "NCI:C34784",
