    rdfs:label "dengue hemorrhagic fever"@en ;
    obo:IAO_0000115 "A dengue disease that occurs when a person experiences a second infection with a heterologous Dengue virus (Orthoflavivirus denguei) serotype, which is transmitted_by Aedes mosquito bite. The infection has_symptom hemorrhagic lesions of the skin, has_symptom thrombocytopenia, has_symptom reduction in the fluid part of the blood, and has_symptom high fever. Four distinct Dengue virus serotypes have been identified."@en ;
